1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,500
A proposition is a statement that is either true or false.

2
00:00:05,500 --> 00:00:11,000
Seven is prime: a proposition, and it is true.

3
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:16,000
Two plus two equals five: also a proposition, and false.

4
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:22,000
Close the door, and x plus one equals three: not propositions yet.

5
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:27,000
NOT P flips the value: true becomes false, false becomes true.

6
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:32,000
P AND Q is true in exactly one row: both true.

7
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:38,000
P OR Q is true in three rows: at least one of them is true.

8
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:44,000
Four rows, because two variables give two to the power two combinations.

9
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:50,000
Read a table by columns, not by rows: each column is one formula.

10
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:58,000
These three columns are the whole vocabulary you will reuse all lesson.

11
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:04,000
P implies Q: if P then Q. P is the hypothesis, Q the conclusion.

12
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:10,000
Only one row is false: P true and Q false.

13
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:18,000
A promise: if you score above ninety, I will gift you a cycle.

14
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:24,000
When the hypothesis is false, the implication is true. This is vacuous truth.

15
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:30,000
P implies Q has exactly the column of NOT P or Q.

16
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:36,000
Four English phrasings that all mean P implies Q.

17
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:41,000
Converse: swap the ends, Q implies P.

18
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:47,000
Inverse: negate both ends, NOT P implies NOT Q.

19
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:54,000
Contrapositive: swap the ends and negate both, NOT Q implies NOT P.

20
00:01:54,000 --> 00:02:01,000
The contrapositive matches the original in all four rows.

21
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:10,000
The converse and the inverse each differ from the original in two rows.

22
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:15,000
Exclusive or is true when exactly one of the two is true.

23
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:20,000
The biconditional P if and only if Q is true when the two agree.

24
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:26,000
So the biconditional is the negation of exclusive or, in every row.

25
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:33,000
Precedence: NOT binds tightest, then AND, then OR, then implies, then iff.

26
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:40,000
Implication is right associative: P implies Q implies R means P implies, Q implies R.

27
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:46,000
A tautology is true in every row. P or NOT P is the model.

28
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:51,000
A contradiction is false in every row. P and NOT P is the model.

29
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:57,000
Anything else is a contingency: true in some rows, false in others.

30
00:02:57,000 --> 00:03:06,000
The decision procedure: write every row, then read the last column.

31
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:12,000
Two formulas are logically equivalent when their columns are identical.

32
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:19,000
De Morgan, first law: NOT of P and Q is NOT P or NOT Q.

33
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:26,000
De Morgan, second law: NOT of P or Q is NOT P and NOT Q.

34
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:36,000
Distribution works, and the two sides need all eight rows of three variables to prove it.

35
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:42,000
An argument is valid when the premises cannot all be true while the conclusion is false.

36
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:49,000
Modus ponens: P implies Q, and P, therefore Q. Valid.

37
00:03:49,000 --> 00:03:56,000
Modus tollens: P implies Q, and NOT Q, therefore NOT P. Also valid.

38
00:03:56,000 --> 00:04:04,000
Affirming the consequent: P implies Q, and Q, therefore P. Invalid.

39
00:04:04,000 --> 00:04:12,000
Denying the antecedent fails for the same row, and one counterexample settles it.

40
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:18,000
Satisfiable means some row makes it true. Unsatisfiable means no row does.

41
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:25,000
With n variables there are two to the n rows, so three variables give eight.

42
00:04:25,000 --> 00:04:31,000
There are sixteen different truth tables on two variables, and 256 on three.

43
00:04:31,000 --> 00:04:38,000
That count is why questions ask how many functions or how many rows, not which one.

44
00:04:38,000 --> 00:04:43,000
One: an implication is false in exactly one row.

45
00:04:43,000 --> 00:04:48,000
Two: contrapositive is equivalent, converse and inverse are not.

46
00:04:48,000 --> 00:04:54,000
Three: remove an arrow by writing NOT P or Q.

47
00:04:54,000 --> 00:05:00,000
Four: a form is invalid the moment one row breaks it.

